// Replication from reflection (Rhobots §8). With
//
//     D = for(y <- x){ x!(*y) | *y }
//
// the pair  x!(D | P) | D  behaves as !P: after one comm the sender-waiter
// pair re-forms and one more copy of P joins the live plane. Two
// substitutions happen in the continuation -- the *y inside the new sender's
// payload rebuilds that payload, and the full-size *y releases D | P onto the
// live plane.
//
// This is the spec's first acceptance test: if it is legible in the scene,
// the metaphor is sound.

new x in {
    for(y <- x){ x!(*y) | *y }
  | x!( for(y <- x){ x!(*y) | *y } | stdout!(Nil) )
}
